card.statement:
(1)

If $|X_{\ell}|=0$ then $R^{f}_{\ell}$ is a semisimple category with a unique indecomposable (=irreducible) module;

(2)

If $|X_{\ell}|=1$ then $R^{f}_{\ell}$ has finite representation type;

(3)

If $|X_{\ell}|=2$ then $R^{f}_{\ell}$ has tame representation type if and only if $|I_{k}|=1$ for all $k\in X$. Otherwise, $R^{f}_{\ell}$ has wild representation type;

(4)

If $|X_{\ell}|>2$ then $R^{f}_{\ell}$ has wild representation type.
